{"id": "batch-1793402637-ZsFz6JBi6zA8omEt9Z6f", "object": "batch", "endpoint": "/v1/messages", "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-5.5-20260921", "completion_window": "24h", "status": "completed", "created_at": 1793402637, "finalized_at": 1793403097, "provider": "Anthropic", "expires_at": 1793489037, "request_counts": {"total": 1, "completed": 1, "failed": 0}, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 1426, "completion_tokens": 994, "total_tokens": 2420, "cost": 0.012792, "is_byok": false}, "error": null, "results": [{"id": "msg_011CgZHSH9NuAfZMUXvmgkxt", "custom_id": "u0000", "response": {"status_code": 200, "request_id": null, "body": {"id": "msg_batch-1793402637-ZsFz6JBi6zA8omEt9Z6f:u0000", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "container": null, "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "I'm weighing whether a burn wound necessarily has a disposition toward infection, since tendencies in MILD might be a subclass of disposition but aren't guaranteed to hold universally. I'm leaning toward being strict and not asserting this relation without stronger certainty, drawing an analogy to how not every risk entails its realization.\n\nFor the diabetic foot ulcer and amputation risk, I'm questioning whether the ulcer itself is the correct bearer of that tendency, since amputation risk seems to inhere in the organism or limb rather than the wound — suggesting this relation may have the wrong bearer and should be marked no.\n\nFor rows 1 and 2, the wound itself seems like the right bearer for an infecting tendency, since both burns and chronic wounds compromise the skin barrier, making infection plausibly true for each — I'll mark these yes.\n\n", "signature": ".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMTpiYXRjaHxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}, {"type": "text", "text": "{\"answers\":[{\"row\":1,\"verdict\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"Every burn wound breaches the skin barrier, so it bears a tendency to become infected, and a tendency is a kind of disposition borne by the wound itself.\"},{\"row\":2,\"verdict\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"Every chronic wound is an open, non-healing wound that bears a tendency to become infected, and that tendency, a disposition, depends on the wound as its bearer.\"},{\"row\":3,\"verdict\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Amputation risk is borne by the patient or the limb that would be amputated, not by the ulcer itself, so this is the wrong bearer.\"},{\"row\":4,\"verdict\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Pressure ulcer risk is borne by a patient before any ulcer develops, so an existing pressure ulcer is the wrong bearer and the statement is nearly circular.\"}]}", "citations": []}], "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-5.5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_details": null, "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1426, "output_tokens": 994, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 706}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": null, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}, "error": null}]}